> In a world of plain reciprocators, who repay like with like, players who simply always cooperate do at least as well. They drift into the population unnoticed, and then defectors feed on them. Against this machine, a player who always cooperates never gets through the opening (the second game above), so that door is shut. A player who always defects does get through the opening, but earns less by it than the machines earn from each other. Against this machine the player who always defects collects the 5 only every third round (the third game above): 7 points in three rounds, where two of the machines collect 9 each from one another. So among these machines the defector falls behind.
